  "contraception": {
    "about": "A drug is a hormonal contraceptive when its own label's uses say it prevents pregnancy, and it contains an estrogen or a progestin. With an estrogen it is combined, since no contraceptive is an estrogen alone; with a progestin and no estrogen it is progestin-only. Only the label's indications and Drug Facts purpose are read, so a drug that mentions contraception elsewhere is not one.",
